  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-08-18T22:32:01.205Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I'm pretty sure a lot of people can agree that VRChat lost its charm as a platform for people almost as soon as the Sunday Meetups got cancelled in December, which eventually led to a huge wave of toxicity. A few months later, after the January memes became irrelevant, we started to notice new memes with direct references to the VRChat staff, including VR Pill and Tupper, because the new community members weren't there during weekly meetups and didn't appreciate the work that was put into them. Of course, it is understandable that VRChat needed a short break while there were too many people using the servers, but most of those issues are already gone, and now it seems like the VRChat team doesn't care about their PR anymore, which isn't what many of us would like to say in reality, and I'm convinced that the staff members, especially VR Pill who is remembered among the originals as the face of justice and humanity, don't deserve the memes that I personally find offensive in a way. \n\nI suggest bringing back the meetups to assure users that VRChat cares about them. It doesn't mean that everyone has to be in VRChat for these events, and I'm sure a lot of people would prefer watching a Twitch stream instead. It may not look like an important thing to the VRChat team who are probably busy enough working on something so big we haven't heard anything exciting in regards to progress on new updates in a long time, which probably means something, despite the lack of public information, but I believe it would decrease the toxicity, and this is exactly what everyone in VRChat needs right now — a better community.",
